{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_prediction_s78_item3_klever_eigenindex_lever", "label": "The eigenindex lever test (poisoning eigen_sr)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "solve_one does not select an eigenvalue by index: it brackets from eigen_sr and bisects to a zero of log(nrm), with the node count checked by the caller. k is implicit, set by the bracket seeded from (n,l) and by which zero the bisection lands on, so the only lever is n \u2014 and n is passed POSITIONALLY, so the poison must wrap the module-level name.", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S78-ITEM3-KLEVER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s78_item3_klever_f54_2", "label": "F54.2 \u2014 patching a positional default is a dead lever", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S78-ITEM3-KLEVER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s78_item3_klever_rung_b", "label": "Rung B \u2014 the eigenindex selector", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Rung B would choose eps_k of the radial Fock operator directly so Courant-Fischer applies at fixed field. A PASS here does not build Rung B; it only shows the quantity Rung B would vary is a live input. A VOID would mean Rung B cannot be built on this solver.", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S78-ITEM3-KLEVER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_prediction_s78_item3_klever_eigenindex_lever", "target": "recovered_prediction_s78_item3_klever_f54_2", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S78-ITEM3-KLEVER.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_prediction_s78_item3_klever_eigenindex_lever", "target": "recovered_prediction_s78_item3